values ('a8e3c1d6-5b47-4f09-9a28-1d0e6c4b7f35', 'introduction-to-nutrition', 'Introduction to Nutrition', 'This course introduces the science of human nutrition and its application to food choices, dietary patterns, health promotion, and disease prevention. Students study digestion and absorption; carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, vitamins, minerals, water, and energy metabolism; dietary reference values and guidance; food labels and composition data; dietary assessment; lifecycle needs; supplements and food safety; chronic disease; culture, behavior, equity, and food systems; and nutrition misinformation. A final diet-analysis project develops quantitative, ethical, and evidence-communication skills using de-identified or simulated intake data.');

