  'Introduction to Nutrition',
  'This course introduces the science of human nutrition and its application to food choices, dietary patterns, health promotion, and disease prevention. Students study digestion and absorption; carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, vitamins, minerals, water, and energy metabolism; dietary reference values and guidance; food labels and composition data; dietary assessment; lifecycle needs; supplements and food safety; chronic disease; culture, behavior, equity, and food systems; and nutrition misinformation. A final diet-analysis project develops quantitative, ethical, and evidence-communication skills using de-identified or simulated intake data.',
  $itnjson${"slug": "introduction-to-nutrition", "title": "Introduction to Nutrition", "description": "This course introduces the science of human nutrition and its application to food choices, dietary patterns, health promotion, and disease prevention. Students study digestion and absorption; carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, vitamins, minerals, water, and energy metabolism; dietary reference values and guidance; food labels and composition data; dietary assessment; lifecycle needs; supplements and food safety; chronic disease; culture, behavior, equity, and food systems; and nutrition misinformation. A final diet-analysis project develops quantitative, ethical, and evidence-communication skills using de-identified or simulated intake data.", "topics": [{"id": "bb320db5-db41-4882-96eb-3856c545792f", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Science, Evidence, and Professional Foundations", "description": "This opening section defines nutrition as an interdisciplinary science connecting food, nutrients, physiology, behavior, environments, and health. Students learn how nutrition knowledge is produced, evaluated, communicated, and used responsibly.", "children": [{"id": "5c054991-f487-4799-9784-e51d60dfae60", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What nutrition science studies", "description": "Students distinguish nutrients, foods, dietary patterns, and food systems while recognizing that health has many interacting causes.", "children": [{"id": "8e852a8b-725c-4db2-a740-71c464d5b471", "type": "concept", "title": "Essential and nonessential nutrients; macronutrients, micronutrients, water, fiber, bioactive compounds, and food matrices"}, {"id": "37932754-e2fb-4504-a884-d73cb4c5d217", "type": "concept", "title": "Nutrient deficiency, inadequacy, excess, toxicity, balance, adaptation, and individual variability"}, {"id": "35cfe974-3f26-4bad-b9f5-eed49eb29da3", "type": "concept", "title": "Biological, behavioral, social, cultural, commercial, environmental, and policy influences on food and health"}]}, {"id": "0c5edd13-7593-41c4-bc64-662f6b639444", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scientific reasoning and study designs", "description": "Students learn what different kinds of research can and cannot establish.", "children": [{"id": "658b8f5e-6c6e-4a3b-82df-1ae0c441f928", "type": "concept", "title": "Question, hypothesis, exposure, intervention, comparator, outcome, mechanism, confounder, mediator, and effect modifier"}, {"id": "6caf18c3-f01c-4970-9024-7a5253404756", "type": "concept", "title": "Laboratory, animal, cross-sectional, case-control, cohort, randomized trial, systematic review, meta-analysis, and guideline"}, {"id": "bdf54c1a-98d8-4782-9488-6956ec5ad8fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Association versus causation; randomization, blinding, adherence, measurement error, bias, uncertainty, replication, and generalizability"}]}, {"id": "e6e20e80-5add-4e90-a496-3166379e0bb4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based and ethical practice", "description": "Students use credible evidence without overstepping the scope of an introductory course or offering individualized medical advice.", "children": [{"id": "d7651176-bbde-42e5-913a-ecc9f781d85e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hierarchy and fit-for-purpose evidence; absolute versus relative effects; statistical versus practical significance"}, {"id": "4bf83ddf-c317-4ee1-9185-d1a21bb307c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional scope, referral to registered dietitian nutritionists and other clinicians, conflicts of interest, and respectful communication"}, {"id": "9442149e-bb6c-413d-82f8-143a2e699b20", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, weight stigma, eating-disorder sensitivity, cultural humility, and avoiding moral labels for foods or people"}]}]}, {"id": "e9f097b1-86e6-4e25-b206-f726bd46d5f7", "type": "topic", "title": "Dietary Reference Values, Guidance, and Healthy Patterns", "description": "Dietary guidance translates evidence into population recommendations, but it is not identical to an individual prescription. Students learn to compare reference values and food-pattern models across contexts.", "children": [{"id": "12351e2e-0fb3-4f36-a73b-afccf495eec2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary Reference Intakes and related values", "description": "Students learn which reference value answers which question and why one number does not fit everyone.", "children": [{"id": "f4f2aee1-4821-4e74-8adb-a83cfbedce37", "type": "concept", "title": "EAR, RDA, AI, UL, CDRR, AMDR, EER, and life-stage groups"}, {"id": "58553931-f082-43c7-b138-c6b5da12cff4", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability of adequacy, group versus individual use, usual intake, day-to-day variation, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "bf1cea6c-42c4-4acf-b6fc-feeecfc3325e", "type": "concept", "title": "Dietary Reference Intakes versus Daily Values on labels and population goals in guidelines"}]}, {"id": "6cb1f346-e057-40d1-954e-60b6894e56ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food-based dietary guidance", "description": "Students examine how countries convert nutrition science into practical messages and policy.", "children": [{"id": "ad9c671f-beed-4b90-b1c6-335ca5f999ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Current Dietary Guidelines for Americans, food-pattern models, visual guides, and country-specific recommendations"}, {"id": "5a9d1eed-74af-4836-832c-6ae8eec185ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Adequacy, balance, moderation, diversity, nutrient density, proportionality, and food safety"}, {"id": "aa1ad5b9-1f3b-4d98-b81a-e8d8e8e83d20", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence review, expert committees, policy context, implementation, updates, and comparison across guidance systems"}]}, {"id": "cc703c03-5002-486a-81fd-a693714fff63", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Healthy dietary patterns in context", "description": "Students focus on overall patterns while respecting culture, budget, access, preference, and health needs.", "children": [{"id": "678c12bf-9fb4-453b-a39c-b6883b8870c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediterranean-style, DASH-style, vegetarian/vegan, traditional and Indigenous foodways, and other culturally grounded patterns"}, {"id": "38757790-5cb0-4550-94e1-75bf9b3fd5a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Vegetables, fruits, whole grains, legumes, nuts/seeds, protein foods, dairy or fortified alternatives, oils, and beverages"}, {"id": "21f01b92-e888-4d95-9564-5ae58d79cb61", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimally processed and ultra-processed food concepts, pattern quality, substitution, meal structure, sustainability, and limitations of labels"}]}]}, {"id": "2f323923-f2ec-4acb-8556-bff086a9deda", "type": "topic", "title": "Digestion, Absorption, Transport, and the Gut Microbiome", "description": "Nutrition begins with food but depends on mechanical, chemical, microbial, and physiological processes that make nutrients available to tissues. This section provides the body-system foundation needed for later nutrient topics.", "children": [{"id": "3db41d94-a2e2-4f95-ba8e-4d13bb7297a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gastrointestinal anatomy and digestion", "description": "Students trace food through the digestive tract and connect organ function to nutrient breakdown.", "children": [{"id": "6f3195d1-8106-4be2-913f-0902ed63439e", "type": "concept", "title": "Mouth, esophagus, stomach, small intestine, large intestine, rectum, liver, gallbladder, and pancreas"}, {"id": "232b8edd-5aa3-466b-bd37-3d0ed62c0d95", "type": "concept", "title": "Motility, chewing, swallowing, acid, bicarbonate, bile, digestive enzymes, mucus, and intestinal surface area"}, {"id": "ecf87252-7ea2-4998-a557-255625a46e42", "type": "concept", "title": "Cephalic, gastric, and intestinal phases; neural and hormonal regulation; common symptom terminology without diagnosis"}]}, {"id": "0ded6d88-0e92-4d1a-b86c-914ba82d7e6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Absorption, transport, and metabolism overview", "description": "Students learn how nutrients cross the intestinal wall, enter circulation, reach tissues, and are stored or excreted.", "children": [{"id": "9206af2a-7dd6-4d4c-8ca9-89e602d88f03", "type": "concept", "title": "Passive diffusion, facilitated transport, active transport, endocytosis, and competition/interactions"}, {"id": "df644223-5f5c-455d-8235-22cd2581dbbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Portal circulation, lymphatic transport, chylomicrons, liver first pass, carrier proteins, storage, and renal excretion"}, {"id": "9105cc46-3291-486e-b99a-d38b068094bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Fed and fasting states; anabolism, catabolism, homeostasis, and metabolic integration"}]}, {"id": "5f7b9d51-1b71-4cd0-9839-3d8d9b8f0058", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gut microbiome and gastrointestinal health", "description": "Students examine the microbiome as a dynamic ecosystem while avoiding exaggerated claims.", "children": [{"id": "d6c9b2d9-21f9-4a14-aa24-110aca7f6f9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Microbiota, microbiome, diversity, resilience, colonization, and host-microbe interactions"}, {"id": "c58b31f4-4aa5-4257-b71f-dfd538753400", "type": "concept", "title": "Fermentable carbohydrate, short-chain fatty acids, bile acids, barrier function, and immune signaling"}, {"id": "957d86e5-37f5-4227-8e3b-c8af43862610", "type": "concept", "title": "Prebiotics, probiotics, fermented foods, synbiotics, antibiotics, evidence limits, and person-to-person variation"}]}]}, {"id": "1413acf6-8868-4273-a476-8dcb66790d38", "type": "topic", "title": "Carbohydrates, Fiber, and Glycemic Physiology", "description": "Carbohydrates are major energy sources and structural components of many foods. Students learn to distinguish carbohydrate types, food sources, digestion, metabolic roles, and health implications.", "children": [{"id": "88391760-36d1-4b2c-9d43-e6a3d14a9412", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carbohydrate chemistry and food sources", "description": "Students connect molecular structure to digestion, sweetness, texture, and dietary quality.", "children": [{"id": "cf274482-abb8-456e-9f12-e5733f0f49ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Monosaccharides, disaccharides, oligosaccharides, starch, glycogen, and non-starch polysaccharides"}, {"id": "e4e86f15-6220-4834-8b0f-14ef11cfa18e", "type": "concept", "title": "Whole grains, legumes, vegetables, fruits, dairy, added sugars, refined grains, and sugar-sweetened beverages"}, {"id": "d534c118-1d51-43dd-9da0-31f154a341a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Total carbohydrate, added versus naturally occurring sugars, whole versus refined grain, and food matrix"}]}, {"id": "21dfdf20-3d05-4a89-9c0f-800fd5de7073", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, absorption, and glucose regulation", "description": "Students follow carbohydrate from digestion to cellular use and storage.", "children": [{"id": "9ad320d2-4639-4db2-98a5-ebf03f786c83", "type": "concept", "title": "Salivary and pancreatic amylase, brush-border enzymes, glucose/galactose/fructose transport, and lactose maldigestion"}, {"id": "9dae4ca1-5bfb-47d5-aded-efcf83faa552", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood glucose, insulin, glucagon, liver/muscle glycogen, glycolysis overview, gluconeogenesis, and ketosis context"}, {"id": "d4b5a448-867d-432f-9c39-16fa7a318fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Glycemic response, glycemic index/load, mixed meals, preparation, individual variability, and measurement limits"}]}, {"id": "4aba78c6-b77d-47ed-a176-88a62d9d1df3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary fiber and health", "description": "Students learn that fibers differ in viscosity, fermentability, solubility, source, and physiological effect.", "children": [{"id": "d96acddb-d646-4d50-96d8-63a78e277a6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Soluble/insoluble, viscous/nonviscous, fermentable/nonfermentable classifications"}, {"id": "b817c193-55d6-4b66-8206-a06217530308", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowel function, satiety, cholesterol, glucose response, microbiome fermentation, and cardiometabolic associations"}, {"id": "571e1ed8-cc48-4731-b0ed-920e2b2605d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Food sources, gradual increase, fluid, tolerability, isolated/functional fibers, label claims, and evidence"}]}]}, {"id": "b49de65b-2781-4c7b-8498-9b39f3660f23", "type": "topic", "title": "Lipids, Essential Fatty Acids, and Cardiometabolic Health", "description": "Dietary lipids provide concentrated energy, essential fatty acids, cell-membrane components, signaling molecules, and carriers for fat-soluble vitamins. Students learn why fat type and food source matter.", "children": [{"id": "1adca155-3a8a-4d5b-82a1-608e7cb7e802", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lipid classes and food sources", "description": "Students distinguish major lipid molecules and relate them to foods and functions.", "children": [{"id": "24c6d68e-207c-47c0-81e2-c83b0e1399c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Fatty acids, triacylglycerols, phospholipids, sterols, and fat-soluble compounds"}, {"id": "767d4ee4-5e0c-408c-90e2-49d96007bcc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain length, saturation, cis/trans configuration, omega families, and essential fatty acids"}, {"id": "7ff710ba-03a8-4b6c-818d-61cad610ffc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Oils, nuts/seeds, fish, dairy, meat, eggs, avocados, processed foods, and hidden fats"}]}, {"id": "5c572dc2-a5be-400f-9ea5-f61e0af6f8be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, transport, and metabolism", "description": "Students trace emulsification, absorption, lipoprotein transport, storage, and mobilization.", "children": [{"id": "caa30cad-0b75-48e6-ba39-d4ff5d990f6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Bile, pancreatic lipase, micelles, enterocytes, re-esterification, chylomicrons, and lymph"}, {"id": "ef10ba7b-d53f-4569-b9a8-9fc722b10b0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lipoprotein roles at an introductory level: chylomicrons, VLDL, LDL, and HDL"}, {"id": "e84e8bf1-a277-4336-a397-734b8a76fb1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Adipose storage, lipolysis, beta-oxidation overview, ketone production, and essential-fatty-acid derivatives"}]}, {"id": "7ca7b679-6abc-444b-8686-157ee61c37b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary fats and health evidence", "description": "Students evaluate substitutions rather than treating a single nutrient in isolation.", "children": [{"id": "f71732b4-b109-4dee-a138-1602c4d55bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Saturated, unsaturated, industrial trans fat, dietary cholesterol, and food-source context"}, {"id": "8e9018d4-d57e-4853-8be7-017955a89a11", "type": "concept", "title": "Replacing saturated fat with unsaturated fat, refined carbohydrate, or other foods; absolute versus relative risk"}, {"id": "54a1c016-0758-47d0-a2c8-7a5f62866308", "type": "concept", "title": "Omega-3 sources, cardiovascular evidence, supplement claims, oxidation, cooking, and moderation"}]}]}, {"id": "4d4e6927-cf0d-4a46-b27e-80cb3dda3f77", "type": "topic", "title": "Proteins, Amino Acids, and Nitrogen Balance", "description": "Protein supports structure, enzymes, transport, immunity, signaling, fluid balance, and tissue turnover. Students learn how protein quantity, quality, distribution, and food source interact with energy intake and life stage.", "children": [{"id": "4476cf8a-2435-4c7a-95b4-458b29429d0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Amino acids and protein structure", "description": "Students understand the building blocks of protein and why sequence and shape determine function.", "children": [{"id": "6d9ecd82-35e6-4897-b5c6-c3b8ab7ec589", "type": "concept", "title": "Essential, nonessential, and conditionally essential amino acids"}, {"id": "a827b5a7-5407-4790-99d9-4f254c63f4a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Peptide bonds; primary through quaternary structure; denaturation and digestion"}, {"id": "d8b007fc-2b50-434f-b16c-8718b0ec12b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural, enzymatic, transport, receptor, antibody, hormonal, contractile, and buffering roles"}]}, {"id": "9e090cc8-f096-4713-9d64-c15ed34c6e45", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, turnover, and nitrogen metabolism", "description": "Students trace protein digestion and the amino-acid pool without treating protein as a storage nutrient.", "children": [{"id": "5ddd06bb-946d-4f3c-b6dc-9a8516c32d67", "type": "concept", "title": "Stomach acid/pepsin, pancreatic proteases, brush-border enzymes, absorption, and portal transport"}, {"id": "9cc39924-a4ee-48d5-b832-0d1a4fb03e6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Protein synthesis and breakdown, amino-acid pool, transamination/deamination overview, ammonia, urea, and excretion"}, {"id": "ca5d568c-b8bc-46da-8b19-334aeb507766", "type": "concept", "title": "Nitrogen balance concepts, energy adequacy, fasting, illness, growth, pregnancy, training, and recovery"}]}, {"id": "24fc63d8-96e9-47af-8f86-1737efb6da2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Protein needs, quality, and food patterns", "description": "Students compare sources and planning strategies across omnivorous and plant-based diets.", "children": [{"id": "5ad9192d-9684-43ac-ac05-35cf5d6350de", "type": "concept", "title": "RDA and other life-stage/activity contexts; body-size scaling, meal distribution, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "a992d9ee-ce77-406a-a1a2-e7f54ef2d9c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Digestibility, indispensable amino-acid pattern, limiting amino acid, complementarity, and quality metrics overview"}, {"id": "77401f87-83d3-4a5c-8e13-32b3ff647896", "type": "concept", "title": "Legumes, soy, nuts/seeds, grains, dairy, eggs, seafood, meat, alternatives, sustainability, affordability, and food safety"}]}]}, {"id": "a7e53aff-e7c0-4499-9aaa-4109355e7684", "type": "topic", "title": "Energy Metabolism, Energy Balance, and Body Composition", "description": "Energy balance is dynamic: intake, expenditure, physiology, environment, behavior, and adaptation interact over time. Students learn calculation concepts without reducing health or body size to personal willpower.", "children": [{"id": "aa5fb329-febc-4fec-a80d-37aaddfc90ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Energy in food and cellular metabolism", "description": "Students connect food energy to ATP production and recognize the limits of simplified calorie accounting.", "children": [{"id": "0c1c63d4-7ea7-4148-9718-9172ef5a8bd0", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy-yielding nutrients and alcohol; bomb calorimetry versus metabolizable energy"}, {"id": "64cc2958-3e3e-47fd-9c32-bb360741bf72", "type": "concept", "title": "ATP, oxidation-reduction, glycolysis, citric acid cycle, electron transport, and beta-oxidation at a conceptual level"}, {"id": "24e18fb4-7de5-4fa3-9077-cc90a630c20d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fed/fasting transitions, substrate use, respiratory quotient concept, and metabolic flexibility"}]}, {"id": "e6b1f467-a6e3-47ef-8f4c-f8971b4b5fe8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Energy expenditure and requirements", "description": "Students estimate energy needs and interpret the uncertainty around prediction.", "children": [{"id": "bddf6f90-622e-427e-9772-06620527295a", "type": "concept", "title": "Resting metabolic rate, thermic effect of food, physical activity, nonexercise activity, growth, lactation, and adaptive thermogenesis"}, {"id": "321a19ed-db7e-4047-b20c-5555ec70475a", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct/indirect calorimetry, doubly labeled water, predictive equations, activity factors, and wearable-device limitations"}, {"id": "63569f12-e859-42af-8902-fbacd431feb6", "type": "concept", "title": "EER, reference body sizes, individual variation, energy availability, and monitoring over time"}]}, {"id": "186315db-76b3-45b7-9f59-328cfebfcc14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body weight, composition, and respectful assessment", "description": "Students distinguish weight from composition and health while recognizing bias and measurement limitations.", "children": [{"id": "bc7ab0c8-54f6-4fa1-9e1f-a8879df74d8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Adipose tissue, lean tissue, bone, water, distribution, and body-composition change"}, {"id": "392fb68f-1798-4499-8e4c-157affe5d8f0", "type": "concept", "title": "BMI at population versus individual level; waist measures, skinfolds, BIA, DXA, and sources of error"}, {"id": "22957124-6935-4b3a-9ff5-dcf6669493a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Appetite regulation, sleep, stress, medications, genetics, environment, food access, weight cycling, stigma, and eating-disorder risk"}]}]}, {"id": "8d025ba4-1a6d-43b4-b758-d738cb3747ea", "type": "topic", "title": "Vitamins: Functions, Sources, Bioavailability, and Safety", "description": "Vitamins are organic compounds needed in small amounts for metabolism, growth, maintenance, and health. Students learn common principles first, then organize individual vitamins by function, source, vulnerability, and risk.", "children": [{"id": "8ee87402-b4ac-4634-a43a-3c6a192ddf0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fat-soluble vitamins", "description": "Students compare absorption, storage, deficiency, and toxicity for vitamins A, D, E, and K.", "children": [{"id": "53c72e7f-3d95-40c9-974a-6c9ccc8b29c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin A: vision, epithelial function, immunity, retinoids/carotenoids, sources, deficiency, and teratogenic toxicity"}, {"id": "6afff98c-78d2-4a14-adf2-9538a70f3e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin D: calcium/phosphorus regulation, skin synthesis, sources, status, deficiency risk, and excess"}, {"id": "c493cf04-4330-464b-93e7-1e1f29370c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin E: antioxidant function and sources; vitamin K: clotting/bone proteins, sources, gut contribution, and medication interactions"}]}, {"id": "3a39c9bd-bde7-48f7-bfd5-8c1d0971b5d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water-soluble vitamins", "description": "Students organize B vitamins and vitamin C around coenzyme roles, blood/cell synthesis, nervous-system function, and antioxidant chemistry.", "children": [{"id": "7570054b-443b-45be-b696-d7fe965d4313", "type": "concept", "title": "Thiamin, riboflavin, niacin, pantothenic acid, biotin, and vitamin B6: coenzyme functions, sources, deficiency patterns, and excess concerns"}, {"id": "9a1acda2-05b3-4adf-9996-d4b3e526fa4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Folate and vitamin B12: one-carbon metabolism, DNA/blood formation, neural health, absorption, deficiency masking, and life-stage issues"}, {"id": "3bedbc47-ee93-4529-b087-bbbb4e0261d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin C: collagen synthesis, antioxidant activity, iron absorption, sources, scurvy, and high-dose limits"}]}, {"id": "7343dea0-8ad3-4bab-9d42-4bc0d036ab56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vitamin assessment and supplementation", "description": "Students distinguish dietary intake, biomarkers, clinical signs, and risk groups before drawing conclusions.", "children": [{"id": "fb6689c0-3f9e-4adf-9b9f-8d1efe9a951b", "type": "concept", "title": "Bioavailability, fortification/enrichment, cooking/storage losses, food matrix, genetics, disease, medications, and interactions"}, {"id": "e77b9ab7-a7c0-4758-a784-05bfcaed30f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet record, status biomarker, functional test, clinical signs, reference ranges, confounding, and interpretation limits"}, {"id": "4e33cd16-7d9b-4b4b-8860-5e7c12d67a58", "type": "concept", "title": "Food-first context, evidence-based indications, dosage, ULs, third-party quality signals, interactions, and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "a714ee1c-9d50-4bf5-8e32-c7070d76fb3d", "type": "topic", "title": "Minerals, Water, Electrolytes, and Fluid Balance", "description": "Minerals and water support structure, fluid distribution, nerve signaling, muscle contraction, oxygen transport, enzymes, and acid-base balance. Students learn that absorption and status depend on chemical form, interactions, regulation, and loss.", "children": [{"id": "596632b7-fe93-4d4b-9377-235c95832972", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major minerals and electrolytes", "description": "Students examine calcium, phosphorus, magnesium, sodium, potassium, chloride, and sulfur as interacting systems.", "children": [{"id": "5bf65839-598b-4fc4-acfd-a0cba2eeefcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bone/mineral structure, ATP and phosphorylation, muscle/nerve function, enzyme roles, and acid-base buffering"}, {"id": "225dc353-437e-4d90-97ed-1f0b83a6eb9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sodium-potassium gradients, blood pressure, fluid compartments, kidney and hormonal regulation, and dietary patterns"}, {"id": "9fab57fc-89ff-4e54-8582-ded98679b91c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sources, absorption, deficiency/excess contexts, processing, salt, and public-health recommendations"}]}, {"id": "ca7f9bc3-17c7-48b3-a9a8-2141b8a9268d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trace minerals", "description": "Students learn key functions, sources, regulation, deficiency patterns, and toxicity concerns for common trace elements.", "children": [{"id": "eea43b44-07ab-49f4-a7bf-29c376ba5475", "type": "concept", "title": "Iron: heme/nonheme absorption, transport, storage, anemia, overload, and life-stage risk"}, {"id": "afcfea5c-7368-4529-acb8-835f2b0b6930", "type": "concept", "title": "Zinc, copper, iodine, selenium, manganese, fluoride, chromium evidence context, molybdenum, and interactions"}, {"id": "157df0ea-247f-435e-9341-ae02446f398a", "type": "concept", "title": "Bioavailability, phytate, vitamin C, enhancers/inhibitors, fortification, environmental exposure, and supplement risk"}]}, {"id": "cbb45d44-8b81-4cbb-8554-6aeb79f7e6ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water and hydration", "description": "Students examine fluid needs and regulation without relying on one universal intake rule.", "children": [{"id": "70eb832a-e6f1-40d1-916a-720b282803f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Body-water compartments, osmolality, thirst, antidiuretic hormone, aldosterone, kidneys, and fluid balance"}, {"id": "dedd311d-0eb4-4ed2-9b21-ed4bf4720ed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Water from beverages/foods, sweat, urine, respiration, gastrointestinal loss, climate, altitude, exercise, fever, and life stage"}, {"id": "3699cfc2-56b4-4ba3-b982-fb7195e48132", "type": "concept", "title": "Dehydration, overhydration/hyponatremia risk, urine and weight indicators, beverage choices, caffeine/alcohol context, and special populations"}]}]}, {"id": "3370bf3e-967a-4571-b0b6-6aaa77f14ae4", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Labels, Food Composition, Portions, and Dietary Assessment", "description": "Food and intake data are measurements, not perfect mirrors of reality. Students learn to read labels, use composition databases, estimate portions, and collect dietary information with appropriate caution.", "children": [{"id": "5513a591-8e6f-4efa-bead-00eb9237290a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nutrition Facts and ingredient labels", "description": "Students interpret label components and distinguish regulated information from marketing.", "children": [{"id": "275c7e2f-ae0b-4226-b9e3-00d8d26d2ebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Serving size, servings per container, calories, nutrients, added sugars, fiber, sodium, %Daily Value, and footnotes"}, {"id": "5bf0994b-3022-4677-b52f-bacfbcd1f506", "type": "concept", "title": "Ingredient order, sub-ingredients, allergens, dates, net quantity, nutrient-content claims, health claims, and structure/function claims"}, {"id": "7896715c-d3c6-4a9c-988b-0a4a15e7e293", "type": "concept", "title": "RDA/AI versus Daily Value, per-serving versus per-package math, label comparisons, front-of-package systems, and jurisdictional differences"}]}, {"id": "076db52c-fc3f-4d57-bbfb-366f3affb5fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food composition and portion estimation", "description": "Students learn where nutrient values come from and why they vary.", "children": [{"id": "64c94443-253e-4a18-82dd-f8aa392ad334", "type": "concept", "title": "USDA FoodData Central data types, analytical versus calculated values, branded foods, missing data, and updates"}, {"id": "3e21c80a-6dbb-47d4-ab93-fbc24a5dc608", "type": "concept", "title": "Edible portion, recipe yield, retention factors, fortification, preparation, variety, season, and sampling variation"}, {"id": "4b657de6-e419-4dc0-a5e2-1019b28b4629", "type": "concept", "title": "Scales, household measures, reference objects, photos, standard portions, restaurant portions, and estimation error"}]}, {"id": "2d2c704d-7fca-4de8-8d6e-51dea2e18d4e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary assessment methods", "description": "Students compare methods by purpose, burden, bias, time frame, and population.", "children": [{"id": "900497de-99a7-4457-a1c2-689a0be8743a", "type": "concept", "title": "24-hour recall, food record, food-frequency questionnaire, screener, diet history, observation, duplicate portion, and biomarkers"}, {"id": "70d930ed-11b2-40dd-963b-3738cd8bf379", "type": "concept", "title": "Usual versus short-term intake, memory, reactivity, under/overreporting, social desirability, portion error, and day-to-day variability"}, {"id": "893aaae6-6416-41a9-804c-9ce7be26fd29", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple-pass methods, repeated days, weekday/weekend/season, database coding, quality checks, privacy, and nonjudgmental interviewing"}]}]}, {"id": "1a0dacf9-d983-42b0-a9a5-8e0922072b8a", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Across the Life Course", "description": "Nutrient and food needs change with growth, reproduction, aging, physiology, activity, and social context. This section introduces lifecycle priorities while reserving clinical prescription for later courses.", "children": [{"id": "18d2a142-1673-40db-94fa-0722b12e126f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pregnancy, lactation, infancy, and early childhood", "description": "Students identify periods of rapid growth and developmental sensitivity.", "children": [{"id": "7b4d3d75-c831-4678-9696-c11699d3ca90", "type": "concept", "title": "Preconception health, gestational changes, folate, iron, iodine, choline, omega-3 context, food safety, nausea, and weight-gain guidance"}, {"id": "76d0d7d4-f631-433d-a772-c5e6c70c3536", "type": "concept", "title": "Lactation physiology, energy/nutrient needs, human milk, formula, vitamin D/iron context, hydration, and support"}, {"id": "e192f263-ba1c-4c85-ae26-d56e2d67d1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Complementary feeding, texture progression, allergens, responsive feeding, choking prevention, growth monitoring, and food security"}]}, {"id": "388056eb-8c6e-4348-9f83-aad7b7c594b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Childhood and adolescence", "description": "Students connect growth, puberty, autonomy, family/school environments, and health behavior.", "children": [{"id": "5b1fd9b9-59c2-4be5-9c95-3ea93dead8e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth patterns, bone accrual, iron, calcium/vitamin D, protein/energy, hydration, and activity"}, {"id": "0d65084e-f4ea-4a87-a27a-fd9f980da1bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Family meals, school food, peers, media, body image, sports, vegetarian patterns, supplements, and caffeine/energy drinks"}, {"id": "6e995cb6-b0ed-4c8f-b494-89b596975609", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive feeding, division of responsibility concepts, neurodiversity/sensory needs, disordered eating signs, and referral"}]}, {"id": "60334331-b351-4027-9634-d3a494287e0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adulthood and older adulthood", "description": "Students examine prevention, function, changing physiology, medications, and social support across adult life.", "children": [{"id": "0a7169ee-aedb-4fae-ba88-bac0e76ffd0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Work/family routines, cardiometabolic health, pregnancy potential, menopause, activity, sleep, alcohol, and food access"}, {"id": "17598004-24b9-4fad-ae6f-e86c19e3b839", "type": "concept", "title": "Sarcopenia, bone health, energy needs, protein distribution, hydration, taste/smell, oral health, dysphagia awareness, and cognition"}, {"id": "1d91bacc-b6f2-4006-a243-962dc7d74da4", "type": "concept", "title": "Polypharmacy, nutrient-drug interactions, food preparation ability, social isolation, congregate meals, and healthy longevity"}]}]}, {"id": "98433649-ee88-4249-b019-ef8355f7b8ed", "type": "topic", "title": "Dietary Patterns and Chronic Disease Prevention", "description": "Chronic diseases develop through interacting genetic, metabolic, behavioral, environmental, and social pathways. Students learn how dietary patterns influence risk without claiming that food alone prevents or cures disease.", "children": [{"id": "88dcb250-ad0f-452f-90c1-a50de09ec472", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardiovascular disease and hypertension", "description": "Students connect dietary patterns and risk factors to atherosclerosis and blood-pressure regulation.", "children": [{"id": "db57e1d9-1372-45cb-b184-92dad5ac56f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood lipids, blood pressure, inflammation context, smoking, activity, sleep, family history, and social conditions"}, {"id": "f42aaa78-9028-44cd-95fa-80d763365cea", "type": "concept", "title": "DASH/Mediterranean-style patterns, unsaturated-fat substitutions, fiber, sodium, potassium-rich foods, and seafood/nuts/legumes"}, {"id": "483ee50f-acd5-40e2-bc7c-9eb7a54ea7bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute risk, prevention versus treatment, biomarkers, medication interaction, and guideline-based referral"}]}, {"id": "cded770a-1945-4631-aac0-ce7f1d0afa5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diabetes, metabolic health, and obesity", "description": "Students examine insulin resistance, glucose regulation, adiposity, and prevention through a non-stigmatizing lens.", "children": [{"id": "a3000273-cb1c-4deb-9ee8-04fa35d2b420", "type": "concept", "title": "Type 1 versus type 2 diabetes overview, prediabetes, insulin resistance, beta-cell function, and glycemic measures"}, {"id": "8dd678c5-b016-4315-b9e3-f02c814fdefb", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet quality, carbohydrate source, fiber, sugary beverages, energy balance, activity, sleep, and weight-independent benefits"}, {"id": "78ca7178-1d52-48bc-8285-7198f57e1ab8", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening, individualized care, medications, social determinants, remission claims, and limits of introductory advice"}]}, {"id": "3b563b86-04a7-4c0e-8f8b-78a1b879e079", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cancer, bone health, and other conditions", "description": "Students evaluate pattern-level evidence, plausible mechanisms, and the danger of single-food cure narratives.", "children": [{"id": "43bc2c31-5712-4498-965c-b381c019806d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cancer prevention evidence: body size, alcohol, processed/red meat, fiber-rich foods, and tobacco/activity context"}, {"id": "2b43cb01-cb02-48d9-a8a3-c85b73b969b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bone health: calcium, vitamin D, protein, activity, hormones, aging, and fracture risk"}, {"id": "25b2e39e-da35-48e0-8154-a9e43c181ce3", "type": "concept", "title": "Gastrointestinal, kidney, liver, neurocognitive, and immune claims as introductory examples requiring condition-specific evidence and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "ee55be61-2c3e-4849-babd-4e7f710503e1", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Safety, Supplements, Functional Foods, and Regulation", "description": "A diet cannot support health if food is unsafe or products are used inappropriately. Students learn foundational hazard control and how conventional foods, fortified foods, supplements, and health claims are regulated differently.", "children": [{"id": "d22b9345-f5b6-4944-a1f7-e1a6dee6eee8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food safety for consumers", "description": "Students identify practical controls for biological, chemical, physical, and allergen hazards.", "children": [{"id": "dfabc09a-fc7b-4a30-bf68-3be6b5062b47", "type": "concept", "title": "Clean, separate, cook, chill; safe sources, hand hygiene, cross-contamination, temperatures, cooling, reheating, storage, and leftovers"}, {"id": "d0f9e67f-3823-43c8-9726-25814bd6bfb5", "type": "concept", "title": "High-risk foods and populations; pregnancy, infants, older adults, immunocompromise, and disaster/power-outage considerations"}, {"id": "f4f4e815-a577-4cdb-bbff-d4f04f7a1187", "type": "concept", "title": "Allergen awareness, recalls, advisories, seafood mercury context, produce washing, home preservation limits, and reliable guidance"}]}, {"id": "bf89a5f8-6884-4836-bc03-37389704b80a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary supplements and fortified products", "description": "Students evaluate need, effectiveness, dose, quality, safety, and interactions before assuming “natural” means safe.", "children": [{"id": "c1b2e947-67f3-44f8-b89c-a4ef8128ca2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamins/minerals, botanicals, amino acids, protein powders, probiotics, omega-3s, sports/weight-loss products, and functional beverages"}, {"id": "f63224b0-5d81-4533-8fd6-9d1d3fbed555", "type": "concept", "title": "Indications, evidence, RDA/AI, UL, dose, form, duration, medication/nutrient interactions, contamination, adulteration, and third-party testing"}, {"id": "82e2cec4-3188-44f3-8b63-908f56eea9a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Food versus supplement labels, fortification/enrichment, bioavailability, regulation, adverse-event reporting, and referral"}]}, {"id": "1c3a35a0-cd0d-4620-9809-17eab948abb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional foods and emerging claims", "description": "Students distinguish a food's nutrient content from a specific demonstrated health effect.", "children": [{"id": "2b886771-f8f7-44bb-b1e4-1d20c4dcc4c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Whole foods, fortified foods, probiotics/prebiotics, plant sterols, bioactives, adaptogen and nootropic claims"}, {"id": "b93b99b3-cf5f-4d1e-b2bc-fec46810186b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanism, dose, matrix, biomarker, clinical outcome, population, comparator, duration, and replication"}, {"id": "78a36893-257c-48f8-86ec-0dd22b5b3ba2", "type": "concept", "title": "Novel foods, personalized nutrition, nutrigenomics awareness, microbiome tests, direct-to-consumer products, ethics, and evidence gaps"}]}]}, {"id": "4442a40f-7cbc-4a7d-8de3-0616a065fe71", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Choice, Behavior, Culture, Equity, and Food Systems", "description": "Eating behavior is shaped by far more than knowledge. Students examine how culture, identity, skills, economics, marketing, access, policy, and food systems influence what people can and choose to eat.", "children": [{"id": "b7ebcea7-dcaf-409d-8d89-923cb1b12704", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Determinants of food choice and eating behavior", "description": "Students explore interacting drivers without reducing decisions to “motivation.”", "children": [{"id": "0eff57c1-1d48-4389-9a3e-f7e5349d13d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Taste, hunger/satiety, habit, reward, stress, sleep, time, cooking skills, convenience, cost, identity, values, and social norms"}, {"id": "206219b2-b564-4d2f-8816-c5c6e14195b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, peers, work/school, retail, restaurants, portion norms, marketing, digital media, and defaults"}, {"id": "33f90778-359c-4e1e-b1dd-e932d51f3e24", "type": "concept", "title": "Behavior-change concepts: capability, opportunity, motivation, self-efficacy, goals, environment design, relapse, and compassion"}]}, {"id": "095c3b4c-28c9-4270-b666-fa446149ad88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culture and inclusive nutrition", "description": "Students treat culturally diverse foodways as complete dietary systems rather than deviations from a default diet.", "children": [{"id": "a7b06841-d17c-46fe-be3e-20b5b83eb12e", "type": "concept", "title": "Staples, mixed dishes, meal timing, commensality, religious practices, migration, acculturation, and food identity"}, {"id": "2327a48a-f791-4bba-9c31-091551aec68a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural humility, listening, pronunciation, translated materials, health literacy, disability access, and avoiding stereotypes"}, {"id": "753e9c0e-5a63-4e58-9dab-fd1bb427de42", "type": "concept", "title": "Adapting guidance through substitution and addition while preserving meaning, affordability, pleasure, and autonomy"}]}, {"id": "4651f160-c119-4f2b-a071-62b47a4c3c0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food security, inequity, and sustainable systems", "description": "Students connect household circumstances and structural conditions to nutrition and environmental outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "4c5ccc95-26ac-42c3-8aa8-d70866eede67", "type": "concept", "title": "Food security dimensions, poverty, housing, transport, healthcare, discrimination, colonization, neighborhood food environments, and policy"}, {"id": "06e19d54-cc70-46b6-818a-69f958139ce6", "type": "concept", "title": "Food assistance, school/community programs, emergency food, mutual aid, local food, and referral resources"}, {"id": "127e5748-811c-4d81-b4b1-1bed984a4e6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Agriculture, labor, climate, biodiversity, land/water, food loss/waste, packaging, life-cycle tradeoffs, and just transitions"}]}]}, {"id": "4a0a3246-a151-4ad6-989d-e431ae9a88a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Misinformation, Media Literacy, and Communication", "description": "Nutrition information travels through research papers, guidelines, news, social media, advertising, and personal stories. Students learn to verify claims, communicate uncertainty, and avoid both credulity and dismissiveness.", "children": [{"id": "362708ec-4e2c-47be-a0e8-b463ab9f3ac0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Claim and source evaluation", "description": "Students use a repeatable process to assess who is making a claim, what evidence supports it, and whether the conclusion fits the data.", "children": [{"id": "cdcb6e39-60a3-4d37-a88b-f5a7aed2e7c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Claim type, source expertise, editorial process, citations, conflicts, product sales, testimonials, and cherry-picking"}, {"id": "90ea6c4f-81dd-4f41-a95c-9a5ceabbdf16", "type": "concept", "title": "Population, exposure/intervention, comparator, outcome, study design, effect size, uncertainty, consistency, and applicability"}, {"id": "78c8ce7c-d72f-489e-8e09-a04498bf113b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanistic plausibility versus human outcomes; surrogate endpoints; preprints; retractions; consensus; and updating beliefs"}]}, {"id": "6abfba52-c1eb-4918-b2c8-49134e8e1017", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common misinformation patterns", "description": "Students recognize recurring rhetorical and statistical tactics.", "children": [{"id": "23d11262-6cf2-4570-9ec4-57289817d2e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-study certainty, “detox,” cure-all, naturalistic fallacy, fear of ingredients, conspiratorial framing, credential inflation, and before/after stories"}, {"id": "a4a40de2-de91-4e84-a6d3-574a8e7d20e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative risk without baseline, correlation as causation, p-hacking awareness, subgroup claims, dose mismatch, animal-to-human leap, and absence of control"}, {"id": "8ece46f9-90ba-42c7-9822-57adad3568c9", "type": "concept", "title": "False balance, headline distortion, influencer sponsorship, affiliate links, AI-generated citations, image manipulation, and algorithmic amplification"}]}, {"id": "ec7e9576-78b2-40fb-8f36-fada805e86b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respectful nutrition communication", "description": "Students translate evidence for different audiences without shame, jargon, or unsupported precision.", "children": [{"id": "d6479bec-e778-4d02-b566-49ac5ae8e6bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain language, teach-back, visuals, numeracy, absolute risk, uncertainty, and actionable options"}, {"id": "63da321c-ad06-4538-908e-66c494455601", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience goals, culture, language, access, disability, health literacy, weight-inclusive language, and trauma sensitivity"}, {"id": "fbd0f6f6-2bb6-44dd-979f-3149b4cf64ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Myth correction, prebunking, empathy, motivational interviewing awareness, boundaries, referral, and documentation of sources"}]}]}, {"id": "f8e65795-7b56-4603-96d6-2346463bf5f8", "type": "topic", "title": "Diet Analysis Project and Integrative Application", "description": "The capstone integrates nutrients, dietary patterns, labels, assessment limitations, context, and evidence. Its purpose is to practice analysis and reflection—not diagnose disease or prescribe a therapeutic diet.", "children": [{"id": "90d5fbaa-b831-411d-a038-12e241a61c1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical data collection and preparation", "description": "Students plan a small diet analysis with informed participation and strong privacy protections.", "children": [{"id": "ec3e7ca4-1868-4d14-ba0e-e46d73e5d0e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-selected or simulated record; consent; opt-out alternatives; de-identification; data minimization; secure storage; and deletion"}, {"id": "03d522fe-7561-42ca-8fc6-a717f6c936a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple nonconsecutive days, weekday/weekend representation, portions, brands, preparation, recipes, beverages, supplements, and context"}, {"id": "3df302ff-e611-46ac-87bd-aa4df9950c9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Eating-disorder/weight-stigma safeguards, no public sharing of individual results, and referral for concerns"}]}, {"id": "43c42152-c2fd-493b-8611-0349f8ac9c57", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analysis and interpretation", "description": "Students compare intake data with appropriate reference values while acknowledging measurement error and day-to-day variation.", "children": [{"id": "a94748cb-283f-44ca-97d3-471fbd29ebe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Data cleaning, FoodData Central or approved software, recipe decomposition, missing foods, assumptions, and quality checks"}, {"id": "4b87bf72-4e70-4197-98f6-4eeda85edc54", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy, macronutrient distribution, fiber, selected vitamins/minerals, food groups/pattern indicators, sodium, added sugars, and saturated fat"}, {"id": "eba1bc4a-94ea-45e3-a6e7-11aa7edf759b", "type": "concept", "title": "DRI/DV/guideline comparison, repeated-day average, uncertainty, under/overreporting, supplement inclusion, and non-diagnostic language"}]}, {"id": "270e29c3-51a0-4040-aff6-f837d5b3ee6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based improvement and reflection", "description": "Students propose feasible pattern-level changes and explain tradeoffs rather than chasing numerical perfection.", "children": [{"id": "ff9bc54b-3254-45a0-826c-b6c1fe43d8d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-first interpretation, substitutions/additions, culture, budget, access, preference, skills, time, sustainability, and safety"}, {"id": "99c2455b-4824-40ff-a264-666d00ea65d7", "type": "concept", "title": "One or two measurable changes, rationale, barriers, support, monitoring, unintended consequences, and when referral is appropriate"}, {"id": "de393f6e-314d-4b85-9a02-953f7e007073", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical report, visual summary, source list, limitations, peer review, reflection, and communication to a defined audience"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$itnjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'introduction-to-nutrition'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Introduction to Nutrition',
  goal = 'Introduction to Nutrition',
  summary = 'This course introduces the science of human nutrition and its application to food choices, dietary patterns, health promotion, and disease prevention. Students study digestion and absorption; carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, vitamins, minerals, water, and energy metabolism; dietary reference values and guidance; food labels and composition data; dietary assessment; lifecycle needs; supplements and food safety; chronic disease; culture, behavior, equity, and food systems; and nutrition misinformation. A final diet-analysis project develops quantitative, ethical, and evidence-communication skills using de-identified or simulated intake data.',
  data = $itnjson${"slug": "introduction-to-nutrition", "title": "Introduction to Nutrition", "description": "This course introduces the science of human nutrition and its application to food choices, dietary patterns, health promotion, and disease prevention. Students study digestion and absorption; carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, vitamins, minerals, water, and energy metabolism; dietary reference values and guidance; food labels and composition data; dietary assessment; lifecycle needs; supplements and food safety; chronic disease; culture, behavior, equity, and food systems; and nutrition misinformation. A final diet-analysis project develops quantitative, ethical, and evidence-communication skills using de-identified or simulated intake data.", "topics": [{"id": "bb320db5-db41-4882-96eb-3856c545792f", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Science, Evidence, and Professional Foundations", "description": "This opening section defines nutrition as an interdisciplinary science connecting food, nutrients, physiology, behavior, environments, and health. Students learn how nutrition knowledge is produced, evaluated, communicated, and used responsibly.", "children": [{"id": "5c054991-f487-4799-9784-e51d60dfae60", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What nutrition science studies", "description": "Students distinguish nutrients, foods, dietary patterns, and food systems while recognizing that health has many interacting causes.", "children": [{"id": "8e852a8b-725c-4db2-a740-71c464d5b471", "type": "concept", "title": "Essential and nonessential nutrients; macronutrients, micronutrients, water, fiber, bioactive compounds, and food matrices"}, {"id": "37932754-e2fb-4504-a884-d73cb4c5d217", "type": "concept", "title": "Nutrient deficiency, inadequacy, excess, toxicity, balance, adaptation, and individual variability"}, {"id": "35cfe974-3f26-4bad-b9f5-eed49eb29da3", "type": "concept", "title": "Biological, behavioral, social, cultural, commercial, environmental, and policy influences on food and health"}]}, {"id": "0c5edd13-7593-41c4-bc64-662f6b639444", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scientific reasoning and study designs", "description": "Students learn what different kinds of research can and cannot establish.", "children": [{"id": "658b8f5e-6c6e-4a3b-82df-1ae0c441f928", "type": "concept", "title": "Question, hypothesis, exposure, intervention, comparator, outcome, mechanism, confounder, mediator, and effect modifier"}, {"id": "6caf18c3-f01c-4970-9024-7a5253404756", "type": "concept", "title": "Laboratory, animal, cross-sectional, case-control, cohort, randomized trial, systematic review, meta-analysis, and guideline"}, {"id": "bdf54c1a-98d8-4782-9488-6956ec5ad8fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Association versus causation; randomization, blinding, adherence, measurement error, bias, uncertainty, replication, and generalizability"}]}, {"id": "e6e20e80-5add-4e90-a496-3166379e0bb4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based and ethical practice", "description": "Students use credible evidence without overstepping the scope of an introductory course or offering individualized medical advice.", "children": [{"id": "d7651176-bbde-42e5-913a-ecc9f781d85e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hierarchy and fit-for-purpose evidence; absolute versus relative effects; statistical versus practical significance"}, {"id": "4bf83ddf-c317-4ee1-9185-d1a21bb307c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional scope, referral to registered dietitian nutritionists and other clinicians, conflicts of interest, and respectful communication"}, {"id": "9442149e-bb6c-413d-82f8-143a2e699b20", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, weight stigma, eating-disorder sensitivity, cultural humility, and avoiding moral labels for foods or people"}]}]}, {"id": "e9f097b1-86e6-4e25-b206-f726bd46d5f7", "type": "topic", "title": "Dietary Reference Values, Guidance, and Healthy Patterns", "description": "Dietary guidance translates evidence into population recommendations, but it is not identical to an individual prescription. Students learn to compare reference values and food-pattern models across contexts.", "children": [{"id": "12351e2e-0fb3-4f36-a73b-afccf495eec2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary Reference Intakes and related values", "description": "Students learn which reference value answers which question and why one number does not fit everyone.", "children": [{"id": "f4f2aee1-4821-4e74-8adb-a83cfbedce37", "type": "concept", "title": "EAR, RDA, AI, UL, CDRR, AMDR, EER, and life-stage groups"}, {"id": "58553931-f082-43c7-b138-c6b5da12cff4", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability of adequacy, group versus individual use, usual intake, day-to-day variation, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "bf1cea6c-42c4-4acf-b6fc-feeecfc3325e", "type": "concept", "title": "Dietary Reference Intakes versus Daily Values on labels and population goals in guidelines"}]}, {"id": "6cb1f346-e057-40d1-954e-60b6894e56ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food-based dietary guidance", "description": "Students examine how countries convert nutrition science into practical messages and policy.", "children": [{"id": "ad9c671f-beed-4b90-b1c6-335ca5f999ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Current Dietary Guidelines for Americans, food-pattern models, visual guides, and country-specific recommendations"}, {"id": "5a9d1eed-74af-4836-832c-6ae8eec185ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Adequacy, balance, moderation, diversity, nutrient density, proportionality, and food safety"}, {"id": "aa1ad5b9-1f3b-4d98-b81a-e8d8e8e83d20", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence review, expert committees, policy context, implementation, updates, and comparison across guidance systems"}]}, {"id": "cc703c03-5002-486a-81fd-a693714fff63", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Healthy dietary patterns in context", "description": "Students focus on overall patterns while respecting culture, budget, access, preference, and health needs.", "children": [{"id": "678c12bf-9fb4-453b-a39c-b6883b8870c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediterranean-style, DASH-style, vegetarian/vegan, traditional and Indigenous foodways, and other culturally grounded patterns"}, {"id": "38757790-5cb0-4550-94e1-75bf9b3fd5a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Vegetables, fruits, whole grains, legumes, nuts/seeds, protein foods, dairy or fortified alternatives, oils, and beverages"}, {"id": "21f01b92-e888-4d95-9564-5ae58d79cb61", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimally processed and ultra-processed food concepts, pattern quality, substitution, meal structure, sustainability, and limitations of labels"}]}]}, {"id": "2f323923-f2ec-4acb-8556-bff086a9deda", "type": "topic", "title": "Digestion, Absorption, Transport, and the Gut Microbiome", "description": "Nutrition begins with food but depends on mechanical, chemical, microbial, and physiological processes that make nutrients available to tissues. This section provides the body-system foundation needed for later nutrient topics.", "children": [{"id": "3db41d94-a2e2-4f95-ba8e-4d13bb7297a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gastrointestinal anatomy and digestion", "description": "Students trace food through the digestive tract and connect organ function to nutrient breakdown.", "children": [{"id": "6f3195d1-8106-4be2-913f-0902ed63439e", "type": "concept", "title": "Mouth, esophagus, stomach, small intestine, large intestine, rectum, liver, gallbladder, and pancreas"}, {"id": "232b8edd-5aa3-466b-bd37-3d0ed62c0d95", "type": "concept", "title": "Motility, chewing, swallowing, acid, bicarbonate, bile, digestive enzymes, mucus, and intestinal surface area"}, {"id": "ecf87252-7ea2-4998-a557-255625a46e42", "type": "concept", "title": "Cephalic, gastric, and intestinal phases; neural and hormonal regulation; common symptom terminology without diagnosis"}]}, {"id": "0ded6d88-0e92-4d1a-b86c-914ba82d7e6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Absorption, transport, and metabolism overview", "description": "Students learn how nutrients cross the intestinal wall, enter circulation, reach tissues, and are stored or excreted.", "children": [{"id": "9206af2a-7dd6-4d4c-8ca9-89e602d88f03", "type": "concept", "title": "Passive diffusion, facilitated transport, active transport, endocytosis, and competition/interactions"}, {"id": "df644223-5f5c-455d-8235-22cd2581dbbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Portal circulation, lymphatic transport, chylomicrons, liver first pass, carrier proteins, storage, and renal excretion"}, {"id": "9105cc46-3291-486e-b99a-d38b068094bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Fed and fasting states; anabolism, catabolism, homeostasis, and metabolic integration"}]}, {"id": "5f7b9d51-1b71-4cd0-9839-3d8d9b8f0058", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gut microbiome and gastrointestinal health", "description": "Students examine the microbiome as a dynamic ecosystem while avoiding exaggerated claims.", "children": [{"id": "d6c9b2d9-21f9-4a14-aa24-110aca7f6f9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Microbiota, microbiome, diversity, resilience, colonization, and host-microbe interactions"}, {"id": "c58b31f4-4aa5-4257-b71f-dfd538753400", "type": "concept", "title": "Fermentable carbohydrate, short-chain fatty acids, bile acids, barrier function, and immune signaling"}, {"id": "957d86e5-37f5-4227-8e3b-c8af43862610", "type": "concept", "title": "Prebiotics, probiotics, fermented foods, synbiotics, antibiotics, evidence limits, and person-to-person variation"}]}]}, {"id": "1413acf6-8868-4273-a476-8dcb66790d38", "type": "topic", "title": "Carbohydrates, Fiber, and Glycemic Physiology", "description": "Carbohydrates are major energy sources and structural components of many foods. Students learn to distinguish carbohydrate types, food sources, digestion, metabolic roles, and health implications.", "children": [{"id": "88391760-36d1-4b2c-9d43-e6a3d14a9412", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carbohydrate chemistry and food sources", "description": "Students connect molecular structure to digestion, sweetness, texture, and dietary quality.", "children": [{"id": "cf274482-abb8-456e-9f12-e5733f0f49ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Monosaccharides, disaccharides, oligosaccharides, starch, glycogen, and non-starch polysaccharides"}, {"id": "e4e86f15-6220-4834-8b0f-14ef11cfa18e", "type": "concept", "title": "Whole grains, legumes, vegetables, fruits, dairy, added sugars, refined grains, and sugar-sweetened beverages"}, {"id": "d534c118-1d51-43dd-9da0-31f154a341a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Total carbohydrate, added versus naturally occurring sugars, whole versus refined grain, and food matrix"}]}, {"id": "21dfdf20-3d05-4a89-9c0f-800fd5de7073", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, absorption, and glucose regulation", "description": "Students follow carbohydrate from digestion to cellular use and storage.", "children": [{"id": "9ad320d2-4639-4db2-98a5-ebf03f786c83", "type": "concept", "title": "Salivary and pancreatic amylase, brush-border enzymes, glucose/galactose/fructose transport, and lactose maldigestion"}, {"id": "9dae4ca1-5bfb-47d5-aded-efcf83faa552", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood glucose, insulin, glucagon, liver/muscle glycogen, glycolysis overview, gluconeogenesis, and ketosis context"}, {"id": "d4b5a448-867d-432f-9c39-16fa7a318fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Glycemic response, glycemic index/load, mixed meals, preparation, individual variability, and measurement limits"}]}, {"id": "4aba78c6-b77d-47ed-a176-88a62d9d1df3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary fiber and health", "description": "Students learn that fibers differ in viscosity, fermentability, solubility, source, and physiological effect.", "children": [{"id": "d96acddb-d646-4d50-96d8-63a78e277a6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Soluble/insoluble, viscous/nonviscous, fermentable/nonfermentable classifications"}, {"id": "b817c193-55d6-4b66-8206-a06217530308", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowel function, satiety, cholesterol, glucose response, microbiome fermentation, and cardiometabolic associations"}, {"id": "571e1ed8-cc48-4731-b0ed-920e2b2605d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Food sources, gradual increase, fluid, tolerability, isolated/functional fibers, label claims, and evidence"}]}]}, {"id": "b49de65b-2781-4c7b-8498-9b39f3660f23", "type": "topic", "title": "Lipids, Essential Fatty Acids, and Cardiometabolic Health", "description": "Dietary lipids provide concentrated energy, essential fatty acids, cell-membrane components, signaling molecules, and carriers for fat-soluble vitamins. Students learn why fat type and food source matter.", "children": [{"id": "1adca155-3a8a-4d5b-82a1-608e7cb7e802", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lipid classes and food sources", "description": "Students distinguish major lipid molecules and relate them to foods and functions.", "children": [{"id": "24c6d68e-207c-47c0-81e2-c83b0e1399c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Fatty acids, triacylglycerols, phospholipids, sterols, and fat-soluble compounds"}, {"id": "767d4ee4-5e0c-408c-90e2-49d96007bcc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain length, saturation, cis/trans configuration, omega families, and essential fatty acids"}, {"id": "7ff710ba-03a8-4b6c-818d-61cad610ffc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Oils, nuts/seeds, fish, dairy, meat, eggs, avocados, processed foods, and hidden fats"}]}, {"id": "5c572dc2-a5be-400f-9ea5-f61e0af6f8be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, transport, and metabolism", "description": "Students trace emulsification, absorption, lipoprotein transport, storage, and mobilization.", "children": [{"id": "caa30cad-0b75-48e6-ba39-d4ff5d990f6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Bile, pancreatic lipase, micelles, enterocytes, re-esterification, chylomicrons, and lymph"}, {"id": "ef10ba7b-d53f-4569-b9a8-9fc722b10b0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lipoprotein roles at an introductory level: chylomicrons, VLDL, LDL, and HDL"}, {"id": "e84e8bf1-a277-4336-a397-734b8a76fb1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Adipose storage, lipolysis, beta-oxidation overview, ketone production, and essential-fatty-acid derivatives"}]}, {"id": "7ca7b679-6abc-444b-8686-157ee61c37b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary fats and health evidence", "description": "Students evaluate substitutions rather than treating a single nutrient in isolation.", "children": [{"id": "f71732b4-b109-4dee-a138-1602c4d55bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Saturated, unsaturated, industrial trans fat, dietary cholesterol, and food-source context"}, {"id": "8e9018d4-d57e-4853-8be7-017955a89a11", "type": "concept", "title": "Replacing saturated fat with unsaturated fat, refined carbohydrate, or other foods; absolute versus relative risk"}, {"id": "54a1c016-0758-47d0-a2c8-7a5f62866308", "type": "concept", "title": "Omega-3 sources, cardiovascular evidence, supplement claims, oxidation, cooking, and moderation"}]}]}, {"id": "4d4e6927-cf0d-4a46-b27e-80cb3dda3f77", "type": "topic", "title": "Proteins, Amino Acids, and Nitrogen Balance", "description": "Protein supports structure, enzymes, transport, immunity, signaling, fluid balance, and tissue turnover. Students learn how protein quantity, quality, distribution, and food source interact with energy intake and life stage.", "children": [{"id": "4476cf8a-2435-4c7a-95b4-458b29429d0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Amino acids and protein structure", "description": "Students understand the building blocks of protein and why sequence and shape determine function.", "children": [{"id": "6d9ecd82-35e6-4897-b5c6-c3b8ab7ec589", "type": "concept", "title": "Essential, nonessential, and conditionally essential amino acids"}, {"id": "a827b5a7-5407-4790-99d9-4f254c63f4a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Peptide bonds; primary through quaternary structure; denaturation and digestion"}, {"id": "d8b007fc-2b50-434f-b16c-8718b0ec12b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural, enzymatic, transport, receptor, antibody, hormonal, contractile, and buffering roles"}]}, {"id": "9e090cc8-f096-4713-9d64-c15ed34c6e45", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digestion, turnover, and nitrogen metabolism", "description": "Students trace protein digestion and the amino-acid pool without treating protein as a storage nutrient.", "children": [{"id": "5ddd06bb-946d-4f3c-b6dc-9a8516c32d67", "type": "concept", "title": "Stomach acid/pepsin, pancreatic proteases, brush-border enzymes, absorption, and portal transport"}, {"id": "9cc39924-a4ee-48d5-b832-0d1a4fb03e6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Protein synthesis and breakdown, amino-acid pool, transamination/deamination overview, ammonia, urea, and excretion"}, {"id": "ca5d568c-b8bc-46da-8b19-334aeb507766", "type": "concept", "title": "Nitrogen balance concepts, energy adequacy, fasting, illness, growth, pregnancy, training, and recovery"}]}, {"id": "24fc63d8-96e9-47af-8f86-1737efb6da2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Protein needs, quality, and food patterns", "description": "Students compare sources and planning strategies across omnivorous and plant-based diets.", "children": [{"id": "5ad9192d-9684-43ac-ac05-35cf5d6350de", "type": "concept", "title": "RDA and other life-stage/activity contexts; body-size scaling, meal distribution, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "a992d9ee-ce77-406a-a1a2-e7f54ef2d9c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Digestibility, indispensable amino-acid pattern, limiting amino acid, complementarity, and quality metrics overview"}, {"id": "77401f87-83d3-4a5c-8e13-32b3ff647896", "type": "concept", "title": "Legumes, soy, nuts/seeds, grains, dairy, eggs, seafood, meat, alternatives, sustainability, affordability, and food safety"}]}]}, {"id": "a7e53aff-e7c0-4499-9aaa-4109355e7684", "type": "topic", "title": "Energy Metabolism, Energy Balance, and Body Composition", "description": "Energy balance is dynamic: intake, expenditure, physiology, environment, behavior, and adaptation interact over time. Students learn calculation concepts without reducing health or body size to personal willpower.", "children": [{"id": "aa5fb329-febc-4fec-a80d-37aaddfc90ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Energy in food and cellular metabolism", "description": "Students connect food energy to ATP production and recognize the limits of simplified calorie accounting.", "children": [{"id": "0c1c63d4-7ea7-4148-9718-9172ef5a8bd0", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy-yielding nutrients and alcohol; bomb calorimetry versus metabolizable energy"}, {"id": "64cc2958-3e3e-47fd-9c32-bb360741bf72", "type": "concept", "title": "ATP, oxidation-reduction, glycolysis, citric acid cycle, electron transport, and beta-oxidation at a conceptual level"}, {"id": "24e18fb4-7de5-4fa3-9077-cc90a630c20d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fed/fasting transitions, substrate use, respiratory quotient concept, and metabolic flexibility"}]}, {"id": "e6b1f467-a6e3-47ef-8f4c-f8971b4b5fe8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Energy expenditure and requirements", "description": "Students estimate energy needs and interpret the uncertainty around prediction.", "children": [{"id": "bddf6f90-622e-427e-9772-06620527295a", "type": "concept", "title": "Resting metabolic rate, thermic effect of food, physical activity, nonexercise activity, growth, lactation, and adaptive thermogenesis"}, {"id": "321a19ed-db7e-4047-b20c-5555ec70475a", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct/indirect calorimetry, doubly labeled water, predictive equations, activity factors, and wearable-device limitations"}, {"id": "63569f12-e859-42af-8902-fbacd431feb6", "type": "concept", "title": "EER, reference body sizes, individual variation, energy availability, and monitoring over time"}]}, {"id": "186315db-76b3-45b7-9f59-328cfebfcc14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body weight, composition, and respectful assessment", "description": "Students distinguish weight from composition and health while recognizing bias and measurement limitations.", "children": [{"id": "bc7ab0c8-54f6-4fa1-9e1f-a8879df74d8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Adipose tissue, lean tissue, bone, water, distribution, and body-composition change"}, {"id": "392fb68f-1798-4499-8e4c-157affe5d8f0", "type": "concept", "title": "BMI at population versus individual level; waist measures, skinfolds, BIA, DXA, and sources of error"}, {"id": "22957124-6935-4b3a-9ff5-dcf6669493a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Appetite regulation, sleep, stress, medications, genetics, environment, food access, weight cycling, stigma, and eating-disorder risk"}]}]}, {"id": "8d025ba4-1a6d-43b4-b758-d738cb3747ea", "type": "topic", "title": "Vitamins: Functions, Sources, Bioavailability, and Safety", "description": "Vitamins are organic compounds needed in small amounts for metabolism, growth, maintenance, and health. Students learn common principles first, then organize individual vitamins by function, source, vulnerability, and risk.", "children": [{"id": "8ee87402-b4ac-4634-a43a-3c6a192ddf0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fat-soluble vitamins", "description": "Students compare absorption, storage, deficiency, and toxicity for vitamins A, D, E, and K.", "children": [{"id": "53c72e7f-3d95-40c9-974a-6c9ccc8b29c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin A: vision, epithelial function, immunity, retinoids/carotenoids, sources, deficiency, and teratogenic toxicity"}, {"id": "6afff98c-78d2-4a14-adf2-9538a70f3e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin D: calcium/phosphorus regulation, skin synthesis, sources, status, deficiency risk, and excess"}, {"id": "c493cf04-4330-464b-93e7-1e1f29370c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin E: antioxidant function and sources; vitamin K: clotting/bone proteins, sources, gut contribution, and medication interactions"}]}, {"id": "3a39c9bd-bde7-48f7-bfd5-8c1d0971b5d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water-soluble vitamins", "description": "Students organize B vitamins and vitamin C around coenzyme roles, blood/cell synthesis, nervous-system function, and antioxidant chemistry.", "children": [{"id": "7570054b-443b-45be-b696-d7fe965d4313", "type": "concept", "title": "Thiamin, riboflavin, niacin, pantothenic acid, biotin, and vitamin B6: coenzyme functions, sources, deficiency patterns, and excess concerns"}, {"id": "9a1acda2-05b3-4adf-9996-d4b3e526fa4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Folate and vitamin B12: one-carbon metabolism, DNA/blood formation, neural health, absorption, deficiency masking, and life-stage issues"}, {"id": "3bedbc47-ee93-4529-b087-bbbb4e0261d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamin C: collagen synthesis, antioxidant activity, iron absorption, sources, scurvy, and high-dose limits"}]}, {"id": "7343dea0-8ad3-4bab-9d42-4bc0d036ab56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vitamin assessment and supplementation", "description": "Students distinguish dietary intake, biomarkers, clinical signs, and risk groups before drawing conclusions.", "children": [{"id": "fb6689c0-3f9e-4adf-9b9f-8d1efe9a951b", "type": "concept", "title": "Bioavailability, fortification/enrichment, cooking/storage losses, food matrix, genetics, disease, medications, and interactions"}, {"id": "e77b9ab7-a7c0-4758-a784-05bfcaed30f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet record, status biomarker, functional test, clinical signs, reference ranges, confounding, and interpretation limits"}, {"id": "4e33cd16-7d9b-4b4b-8860-5e7c12d67a58", "type": "concept", "title": "Food-first context, evidence-based indications, dosage, ULs, third-party quality signals, interactions, and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "a714ee1c-9d50-4bf5-8e32-c7070d76fb3d", "type": "topic", "title": "Minerals, Water, Electrolytes, and Fluid Balance", "description": "Minerals and water support structure, fluid distribution, nerve signaling, muscle contraction, oxygen transport, enzymes, and acid-base balance. Students learn that absorption and status depend on chemical form, interactions, regulation, and loss.", "children": [{"id": "596632b7-fe93-4d4b-9377-235c95832972", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major minerals and electrolytes", "description": "Students examine calcium, phosphorus, magnesium, sodium, potassium, chloride, and sulfur as interacting systems.", "children": [{"id": "5bf65839-598b-4fc4-acfd-a0cba2eeefcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bone/mineral structure, ATP and phosphorylation, muscle/nerve function, enzyme roles, and acid-base buffering"}, {"id": "225dc353-437e-4d90-97ed-1f0b83a6eb9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sodium-potassium gradients, blood pressure, fluid compartments, kidney and hormonal regulation, and dietary patterns"}, {"id": "9fab57fc-89ff-4e54-8582-ded98679b91c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sources, absorption, deficiency/excess contexts, processing, salt, and public-health recommendations"}]}, {"id": "ca7f9bc3-17c7-48b3-a9a8-2141b8a9268d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trace minerals", "description": "Students learn key functions, sources, regulation, deficiency patterns, and toxicity concerns for common trace elements.", "children": [{"id": "eea43b44-07ab-49f4-a7bf-29c376ba5475", "type": "concept", "title": "Iron: heme/nonheme absorption, transport, storage, anemia, overload, and life-stage risk"}, {"id": "afcfea5c-7368-4529-acb8-835f2b0b6930", "type": "concept", "title": "Zinc, copper, iodine, selenium, manganese, fluoride, chromium evidence context, molybdenum, and interactions"}, {"id": "157df0ea-247f-435e-9341-ae02446f398a", "type": "concept", "title": "Bioavailability, phytate, vitamin C, enhancers/inhibitors, fortification, environmental exposure, and supplement risk"}]}, {"id": "cbb45d44-8b81-4cbb-8554-6aeb79f7e6ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water and hydration", "description": "Students examine fluid needs and regulation without relying on one universal intake rule.", "children": [{"id": "70eb832a-e6f1-40d1-916a-720b282803f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Body-water compartments, osmolality, thirst, antidiuretic hormone, aldosterone, kidneys, and fluid balance"}, {"id": "dedd311d-0eb4-4ed2-9b21-ed4bf4720ed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Water from beverages/foods, sweat, urine, respiration, gastrointestinal loss, climate, altitude, exercise, fever, and life stage"}, {"id": "3699cfc2-56b4-4ba3-b982-fb7195e48132", "type": "concept", "title": "Dehydration, overhydration/hyponatremia risk, urine and weight indicators, beverage choices, caffeine/alcohol context, and special populations"}]}]}, {"id": "3370bf3e-967a-4571-b0b6-6aaa77f14ae4", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Labels, Food Composition, Portions, and Dietary Assessment", "description": "Food and intake data are measurements, not perfect mirrors of reality. Students learn to read labels, use composition databases, estimate portions, and collect dietary information with appropriate caution.", "children": [{"id": "5513a591-8e6f-4efa-bead-00eb9237290a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nutrition Facts and ingredient labels", "description": "Students interpret label components and distinguish regulated information from marketing.", "children": [{"id": "275c7e2f-ae0b-4226-b9e3-00d8d26d2ebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Serving size, servings per container, calories, nutrients, added sugars, fiber, sodium, %Daily Value, and footnotes"}, {"id": "5bf0994b-3022-4677-b52f-bacfbcd1f506", "type": "concept", "title": "Ingredient order, sub-ingredients, allergens, dates, net quantity, nutrient-content claims, health claims, and structure/function claims"}, {"id": "7896715c-d3c6-4a9c-988b-0a4a15e7e293", "type": "concept", "title": "RDA/AI versus Daily Value, per-serving versus per-package math, label comparisons, front-of-package systems, and jurisdictional differences"}]}, {"id": "076db52c-fc3f-4d57-bbfb-366f3affb5fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food composition and portion estimation", "description": "Students learn where nutrient values come from and why they vary.", "children": [{"id": "64c94443-253e-4a18-82dd-f8aa392ad334", "type": "concept", "title": "USDA FoodData Central data types, analytical versus calculated values, branded foods, missing data, and updates"}, {"id": "3e21c80a-6dbb-47d4-ab93-fbc24a5dc608", "type": "concept", "title": "Edible portion, recipe yield, retention factors, fortification, preparation, variety, season, and sampling variation"}, {"id": "4b657de6-e419-4dc0-a5e2-1019b28b4629", "type": "concept", "title": "Scales, household measures, reference objects, photos, standard portions, restaurant portions, and estimation error"}]}, {"id": "2d2c704d-7fca-4de8-8d6e-51dea2e18d4e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary assessment methods", "description": "Students compare methods by purpose, burden, bias, time frame, and population.", "children": [{"id": "900497de-99a7-4457-a1c2-689a0be8743a", "type": "concept", "title": "24-hour recall, food record, food-frequency questionnaire, screener, diet history, observation, duplicate portion, and biomarkers"}, {"id": "70d930ed-11b2-40dd-963b-3738cd8bf379", "type": "concept", "title": "Usual versus short-term intake, memory, reactivity, under/overreporting, social desirability, portion error, and day-to-day variability"}, {"id": "893aaae6-6416-41a9-804c-9ce7be26fd29", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple-pass methods, repeated days, weekday/weekend/season, database coding, quality checks, privacy, and nonjudgmental interviewing"}]}]}, {"id": "1a0dacf9-d983-42b0-a9a5-8e0922072b8a", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Across the Life Course", "description": "Nutrient and food needs change with growth, reproduction, aging, physiology, activity, and social context. This section introduces lifecycle priorities while reserving clinical prescription for later courses.", "children": [{"id": "18d2a142-1673-40db-94fa-0722b12e126f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pregnancy, lactation, infancy, and early childhood", "description": "Students identify periods of rapid growth and developmental sensitivity.", "children": [{"id": "7b4d3d75-c831-4678-9696-c11699d3ca90", "type": "concept", "title": "Preconception health, gestational changes, folate, iron, iodine, choline, omega-3 context, food safety, nausea, and weight-gain guidance"}, {"id": "76d0d7d4-f631-433d-a772-c5e6c70c3536", "type": "concept", "title": "Lactation physiology, energy/nutrient needs, human milk, formula, vitamin D/iron context, hydration, and support"}, {"id": "e192f263-ba1c-4c85-ae26-d56e2d67d1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Complementary feeding, texture progression, allergens, responsive feeding, choking prevention, growth monitoring, and food security"}]}, {"id": "388056eb-8c6e-4348-9f83-aad7b7c594b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Childhood and adolescence", "description": "Students connect growth, puberty, autonomy, family/school environments, and health behavior.", "children": [{"id": "5b1fd9b9-59c2-4be5-9c95-3ea93dead8e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth patterns, bone accrual, iron, calcium/vitamin D, protein/energy, hydration, and activity"}, {"id": "0d65084e-f4ea-4a87-a27a-fd9f980da1bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Family meals, school food, peers, media, body image, sports, vegetarian patterns, supplements, and caffeine/energy drinks"}, {"id": "6e995cb6-b0ed-4c8f-b494-89b596975609", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive feeding, division of responsibility concepts, neurodiversity/sensory needs, disordered eating signs, and referral"}]}, {"id": "60334331-b351-4027-9634-d3a494287e0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adulthood and older adulthood", "description": "Students examine prevention, function, changing physiology, medications, and social support across adult life.", "children": [{"id": "0a7169ee-aedb-4fae-ba88-bac0e76ffd0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Work/family routines, cardiometabolic health, pregnancy potential, menopause, activity, sleep, alcohol, and food access"}, {"id": "17598004-24b9-4fad-ae6f-e86c19e3b839", "type": "concept", "title": "Sarcopenia, bone health, energy needs, protein distribution, hydration, taste/smell, oral health, dysphagia awareness, and cognition"}, {"id": "1d91bacc-b6f2-4006-a243-962dc7d74da4", "type": "concept", "title": "Polypharmacy, nutrient-drug interactions, food preparation ability, social isolation, congregate meals, and healthy longevity"}]}]}, {"id": "98433649-ee88-4249-b019-ef8355f7b8ed", "type": "topic", "title": "Dietary Patterns and Chronic Disease Prevention", "description": "Chronic diseases develop through interacting genetic, metabolic, behavioral, environmental, and social pathways. Students learn how dietary patterns influence risk without claiming that food alone prevents or cures disease.", "children": [{"id": "88dcb250-ad0f-452f-90c1-a50de09ec472", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardiovascular disease and hypertension", "description": "Students connect dietary patterns and risk factors to atherosclerosis and blood-pressure regulation.", "children": [{"id": "db57e1d9-1372-45cb-b184-92dad5ac56f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood lipids, blood pressure, inflammation context, smoking, activity, sleep, family history, and social conditions"}, {"id": "f42aaa78-9028-44cd-95fa-80d763365cea", "type": "concept", "title": "DASH/Mediterranean-style patterns, unsaturated-fat substitutions, fiber, sodium, potassium-rich foods, and seafood/nuts/legumes"}, {"id": "483ee50f-acd5-40e2-bc7c-9eb7a54ea7bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute risk, prevention versus treatment, biomarkers, medication interaction, and guideline-based referral"}]}, {"id": "cded770a-1945-4631-aac0-ce7f1d0afa5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diabetes, metabolic health, and obesity", "description": "Students examine insulin resistance, glucose regulation, adiposity, and prevention through a non-stigmatizing lens.", "children": [{"id": "a3000273-cb1c-4deb-9ee8-04fa35d2b420", "type": "concept", "title": "Type 1 versus type 2 diabetes overview, prediabetes, insulin resistance, beta-cell function, and glycemic measures"}, {"id": "8dd678c5-b016-4315-b9e3-f02c814fdefb", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet quality, carbohydrate source, fiber, sugary beverages, energy balance, activity, sleep, and weight-independent benefits"}, {"id": "78ca7178-1d52-48bc-8285-7198f57e1ab8", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening, individualized care, medications, social determinants, remission claims, and limits of introductory advice"}]}, {"id": "3b563b86-04a7-4c0e-8f8b-78a1b879e079", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cancer, bone health, and other conditions", "description": "Students evaluate pattern-level evidence, plausible mechanisms, and the danger of single-food cure narratives.", "children": [{"id": "43bc2c31-5712-4498-965c-b381c019806d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cancer prevention evidence: body size, alcohol, processed/red meat, fiber-rich foods, and tobacco/activity context"}, {"id": "2b43cb01-cb02-48d9-a8a3-c85b73b969b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bone health: calcium, vitamin D, protein, activity, hormones, aging, and fracture risk"}, {"id": "25b2e39e-da35-48e0-8154-a9e43c181ce3", "type": "concept", "title": "Gastrointestinal, kidney, liver, neurocognitive, and immune claims as introductory examples requiring condition-specific evidence and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "ee55be61-2c3e-4849-babd-4e7f710503e1", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Safety, Supplements, Functional Foods, and Regulation", "description": "A diet cannot support health if food is unsafe or products are used inappropriately. Students learn foundational hazard control and how conventional foods, fortified foods, supplements, and health claims are regulated differently.", "children": [{"id": "d22b9345-f5b6-4944-a1f7-e1a6dee6eee8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food safety for consumers", "description": "Students identify practical controls for biological, chemical, physical, and allergen hazards.", "children": [{"id": "dfabc09a-fc7b-4a30-bf68-3be6b5062b47", "type": "concept", "title": "Clean, separate, cook, chill; safe sources, hand hygiene, cross-contamination, temperatures, cooling, reheating, storage, and leftovers"}, {"id": "d0f9e67f-3823-43c8-9726-25814bd6bfb5", "type": "concept", "title": "High-risk foods and populations; pregnancy, infants, older adults, immunocompromise, and disaster/power-outage considerations"}, {"id": "f4f4e815-a577-4cdb-bbff-d4f04f7a1187", "type": "concept", "title": "Allergen awareness, recalls, advisories, seafood mercury context, produce washing, home preservation limits, and reliable guidance"}]}, {"id": "bf89a5f8-6884-4836-bc03-37389704b80a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary supplements and fortified products", "description": "Students evaluate need, effectiveness, dose, quality, safety, and interactions before assuming “natural” means safe.", "children": [{"id": "c1b2e947-67f3-44f8-b89c-a4ef8128ca2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Vitamins/minerals, botanicals, amino acids, protein powders, probiotics, omega-3s, sports/weight-loss products, and functional beverages"}, {"id": "f63224b0-5d81-4533-8fd6-9d1d3fbed555", "type": "concept", "title": "Indications, evidence, RDA/AI, UL, dose, form, duration, medication/nutrient interactions, contamination, adulteration, and third-party testing"}, {"id": "82e2cec4-3188-44f3-8b63-908f56eea9a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Food versus supplement labels, fortification/enrichment, bioavailability, regulation, adverse-event reporting, and referral"}]}, {"id": "1c3a35a0-cd0d-4620-9809-17eab948abb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional foods and emerging claims", "description": "Students distinguish a food's nutrient content from a specific demonstrated health effect.", "children": [{"id": "2b886771-f8f7-44bb-b1e4-1d20c4dcc4c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Whole foods, fortified foods, probiotics/prebiotics, plant sterols, bioactives, adaptogen and nootropic claims"}, {"id": "b93b99b3-cf5f-4d1e-b2bc-fec46810186b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanism, dose, matrix, biomarker, clinical outcome, population, comparator, duration, and replication"}, {"id": "78a36893-257c-48f8-86ec-0dd22b5b3ba2", "type": "concept", "title": "Novel foods, personalized nutrition, nutrigenomics awareness, microbiome tests, direct-to-consumer products, ethics, and evidence gaps"}]}]}, {"id": "4442a40f-7cbc-4a7d-8de3-0616a065fe71", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Choice, Behavior, Culture, Equity, and Food Systems", "description": "Eating behavior is shaped by far more than knowledge. Students examine how culture, identity, skills, economics, marketing, access, policy, and food systems influence what people can and choose to eat.", "children": [{"id": "b7ebcea7-dcaf-409d-8d89-923cb1b12704", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Determinants of food choice and eating behavior", "description": "Students explore interacting drivers without reducing decisions to “motivation.”", "children": [{"id": "0eff57c1-1d48-4389-9a3e-f7e5349d13d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Taste, hunger/satiety, habit, reward, stress, sleep, time, cooking skills, convenience, cost, identity, values, and social norms"}, {"id": "206219b2-b564-4d2f-8816-c5c6e14195b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, peers, work/school, retail, restaurants, portion norms, marketing, digital media, and defaults"}, {"id": "33f90778-359c-4e1e-b1dd-e932d51f3e24", "type": "concept", "title": "Behavior-change concepts: capability, opportunity, motivation, self-efficacy, goals, environment design, relapse, and compassion"}]}, {"id": "095c3b4c-28c9-4270-b666-fa446149ad88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culture and inclusive nutrition", "description": "Students treat culturally diverse foodways as complete dietary systems rather than deviations from a default diet.", "children": [{"id": "a7b06841-d17c-46fe-be3e-20b5b83eb12e", "type": "concept", "title": "Staples, mixed dishes, meal timing, commensality, religious practices, migration, acculturation, and food identity"}, {"id": "2327a48a-f791-4bba-9c31-091551aec68a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural humility, listening, pronunciation, translated materials, health literacy, disability access, and avoiding stereotypes"}, {"id": "753e9c0e-5a63-4e58-9dab-fd1bb427de42", "type": "concept", "title": "Adapting guidance through substitution and addition while preserving meaning, affordability, pleasure, and autonomy"}]}, {"id": "4651f160-c119-4f2b-a071-62b47a4c3c0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food security, inequity, and sustainable systems", "description": "Students connect household circumstances and structural conditions to nutrition and environmental outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "4c5ccc95-26ac-42c3-8aa8-d70866eede67", "type": "concept", "title": "Food security dimensions, poverty, housing, transport, healthcare, discrimination, colonization, neighborhood food environments, and policy"}, {"id": "06e19d54-cc70-46b6-818a-69f958139ce6", "type": "concept", "title": "Food assistance, school/community programs, emergency food, mutual aid, local food, and referral resources"}, {"id": "127e5748-811c-4d81-b4b1-1bed984a4e6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Agriculture, labor, climate, biodiversity, land/water, food loss/waste, packaging, life-cycle tradeoffs, and just transitions"}]}]}, {"id": "4a0a3246-a151-4ad6-989d-e431ae9a88a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Misinformation, Media Literacy, and Communication", "description": "Nutrition information travels through research papers, guidelines, news, social media, advertising, and personal stories. Students learn to verify claims, communicate uncertainty, and avoid both credulity and dismissiveness.", "children": [{"id": "362708ec-4e2c-47be-a0e8-b463ab9f3ac0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Claim and source evaluation", "description": "Students use a repeatable process to assess who is making a claim, what evidence supports it, and whether the conclusion fits the data.", "children": [{"id": "cdcb6e39-60a3-4d37-a88b-f5a7aed2e7c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Claim type, source expertise, editorial process, citations, conflicts, product sales, testimonials, and cherry-picking"}, {"id": "90ea6c4f-81dd-4f41-a95c-9a5ceabbdf16", "type": "concept", "title": "Population, exposure/intervention, comparator, outcome, study design, effect size, uncertainty, consistency, and applicability"}, {"id": "78c8ce7c-d72f-489e-8e09-a04498bf113b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mechanistic plausibility versus human outcomes; surrogate endpoints; preprints; retractions; consensus; and updating beliefs"}]}, {"id": "6abfba52-c1eb-4918-b2c8-49134e8e1017", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common misinformation patterns", "description": "Students recognize recurring rhetorical and statistical tactics.", "children": [{"id": "23d11262-6cf2-4570-9ec4-57289817d2e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-study certainty, “detox,” cure-all, naturalistic fallacy, fear of ingredients, conspiratorial framing, credential inflation, and before/after stories"}, {"id": "a4a40de2-de91-4e84-a6d3-574a8e7d20e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative risk without baseline, correlation as causation, p-hacking awareness, subgroup claims, dose mismatch, animal-to-human leap, and absence of control"}, {"id": "8ece46f9-90ba-42c7-9822-57adad3568c9", "type": "concept", "title": "False balance, headline distortion, influencer sponsorship, affiliate links, AI-generated citations, image manipulation, and algorithmic amplification"}]}, {"id": "ec7e9576-78b2-40fb-8f36-fada805e86b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respectful nutrition communication", "description": "Students translate evidence for different audiences without shame, jargon, or unsupported precision.", "children": [{"id": "d6479bec-e778-4d02-b566-49ac5ae8e6bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain language, teach-back, visuals, numeracy, absolute risk, uncertainty, and actionable options"}, {"id": "63da321c-ad06-4538-908e-66c494455601", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience goals, culture, language, access, disability, health literacy, weight-inclusive language, and trauma sensitivity"}, {"id": "fbd0f6f6-2bb6-44dd-979f-3149b4cf64ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Myth correction, prebunking, empathy, motivational interviewing awareness, boundaries, referral, and documentation of sources"}]}]}, {"id": "f8e65795-7b56-4603-96d6-2346463bf5f8", "type": "topic", "title": "Diet Analysis Project and Integrative Application", "description": "The capstone integrates nutrients, dietary patterns, labels, assessment limitations, context, and evidence. Its purpose is to practice analysis and reflection—not diagnose disease or prescribe a therapeutic diet.", "children": [{"id": "90d5fbaa-b831-411d-a038-12e241a61c1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical data collection and preparation", "description": "Students plan a small diet analysis with informed participation and strong privacy protections.", "children": [{"id": "ec3e7ca4-1868-4d14-ba0e-e46d73e5d0e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-selected or simulated record; consent; opt-out alternatives; de-identification; data minimization; secure storage; and deletion"}, {"id": "03d522fe-7561-42ca-8fc6-a717f6c936a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple nonconsecutive days, weekday/weekend representation, portions, brands, preparation, recipes, beverages, supplements, and context"}, {"id": "3df302ff-e611-46ac-87bd-aa4df9950c9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Eating-disorder/weight-stigma safeguards, no public sharing of individual results, and referral for concerns"}]}, {"id": "43c42152-c2fd-493b-8611-0349f8ac9c57", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analysis and interpretation", "description": "Students compare intake data with appropriate reference values while acknowledging measurement error and day-to-day variation.", "children": [{"id": "a94748cb-283f-44ca-97d3-471fbd29ebe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Data cleaning, FoodData Central or approved software, recipe decomposition, missing foods, assumptions, and quality checks"}, {"id": "4b87bf72-4e70-4197-98f6-4eeda85edc54", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy, macronutrient distribution, fiber, selected vitamins/minerals, food groups/pattern indicators, sodium, added sugars, and saturated fat"}, {"id": "eba1bc4a-94ea-45e3-a6e7-11aa7edf759b", "type": "concept", "title": "DRI/DV/guideline comparison, repeated-day average, uncertainty, under/overreporting, supplement inclusion, and non-diagnostic language"}]}, {"id": "270e29c3-51a0-4040-aff6-f837d5b3ee6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based improvement and reflection", "description": "Students propose feasible pattern-level changes and explain tradeoffs rather than chasing numerical perfection.", "children": [{"id": "ff9bc54b-3254-45a0-826c-b6c1fe43d8d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-first interpretation, substitutions/additions, culture, budget, access, preference, skills, time, sustainability, and safety"}, {"id": "99c2455b-4824-40ff-a264-666d00ea65d7", "type": "concept", "title": "One or two measurable changes, rationale, barriers, support, monitoring, unintended consequences, and when referral is appropriate"}, {"id": "de393f6e-314d-4b85-9a02-953f7e007073", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical report, visual summary, source list, limitations, peer review, reflection, and communication to a defined audience"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$itnjson$::jsonb,
